WEBVTT

00:09.090 --> 00:11.380
They know we're here.
We'll be surrounded soon.

00:13.470 --> 00:15.510
The Imperial Command is ours.
Let's get out of here.

00:17.550 --> 00:19.640
It's not my job to protect you.

00:22.480 --> 00:24.560
So if you want to live, try to keep up.

00:33.990 --> 00:36.700
THE ELUSIVE
SAMURAI

01:56.320 --> 02:00.910
THE ELUSIVE
SAMURAI

02:04.160 --> 02:05.580
When I give the signal,

02:06.080 --> 02:07.330
everyone goes in together.

02:10.580 --> 02:11.590
Damn it.

02:12.840 --> 02:14.550
And take this, too!

02:16.720 --> 02:18.840
I can't see the thieves
in all this smoke and light.

02:18.930 --> 02:20.800
-My eyes!
-Get past the smoke!

02:20.890 --> 02:21.890
Give me that.

02:28.560 --> 02:29.770
I can hear them.

02:31.650 --> 02:32.690
I can hear them.

02:32.770 --> 02:34.230
They used the fire as a distraction,

02:34.320 --> 02:36.110
and they're climbing the wall
on the opposite side.

02:38.530 --> 02:39.530
What…

02:39.610 --> 02:40.700
Damn it.

02:41.280 --> 02:43.700
I'm nowhere near as good with the bow
as Sadamune.

02:43.780 --> 02:45.040
-Let's go!
-Westward!

02:45.120 --> 02:46.700
Where is Sadamune?

02:46.790 --> 02:48.580
The thieves scaled the wall and fled!

02:48.660 --> 02:52.210
Gather your pride as Ogasawara's
retainers and don't let them get away!

02:53.170 --> 02:54.460
That's Genba's signal.

02:55.380 --> 02:57.880
-Time to lure them away.
-Yes.

02:57.970 --> 02:59.930
Over there. They escaped on horseback.

03:00.510 --> 03:02.890
<i>I heard the sound</i>
<i>of horses starting to run,</i>

03:02.970 --> 03:04.970
<i>but there was no sound</i>
<i>of the brats' footsteps</i>

03:05.060 --> 03:07.020
<i>going from the wall to the horse.</i>

03:07.100 --> 03:09.350
<i>The horses probably belong to</i>
<i>their allies,</i>

03:09.430 --> 03:11.400
<i>hidden beforehand as a lure.</i>

03:11.480 --> 03:13.730
<i>And there was no sound</i>
<i>of anyone walking away.</i>

03:14.230 --> 03:16.780
<i>If that's the case,</i>

03:18.320 --> 03:19.780
<i>that means they're very close.</i>

03:21.320 --> 03:22.870
<i>The brats must be in the forest,</i>

03:24.030 --> 03:26.740
<i>holding their breaths.</i>

03:33.500 --> 03:37.670
Where

03:38.590 --> 03:40.340
are

03:41.130 --> 03:43.140
you?

03:43.220 --> 03:47.010
<i>It's Sadamune's suck-up,</i>
<i>Sukefusa Ichikawa.</i>

03:47.100 --> 03:49.140
<i>The guy's got the ears of a fox.</i>
<i>It isn't fair he's hunting us down</i>

03:49.220 --> 03:50.390
<i>on this dark of a night.</i>

03:50.980 --> 03:53.730
<i>My illusions to fool his blind spot</i>
<i>won't help us.</i>

03:54.480 --> 03:57.110
<i>This is bad. We'll be caught at this rate.</i>

03:58.440 --> 04:00.400
<i>Should I sell this kid out at this point?</i>

04:01.320 --> 04:02.780
<i>I messed up.</i>

04:02.860 --> 04:05.530
<i>I thought it'd be fun to teach this naive,</i>
<i>spoiled brat</i>

04:05.620 --> 04:07.490
<i>the harsh realities of the world.</i>

04:17.130 --> 04:18.170
<i>This one…</i>

04:19.090 --> 04:20.340
<i>I'm leaving behind.</i>

04:26.260 --> 04:28.390
<i>If it's just me, I can make it.</i>

04:29.100 --> 04:32.180
-<i>No!</i>
-<i>No one can hear my stealthy steps!</i>

04:32.680 --> 04:33.940
<i>In hide-and-seek,</i>

04:34.020 --> 04:37.060
<i>you'll absolutely be caught</i>
<i>if you move from such a close distance!</i>

04:37.560 --> 04:40.690
NANBOKUCHO GAME OF TAG

04:41.780 --> 04:43.450
I found you.

04:43.530 --> 04:45.200
ALL-HEARING DEMON
SUKEFUSA ICHIKAWA

04:49.160 --> 04:51.080
Ugh. Damn it.

04:51.160 --> 04:53.250
I shouldn't have brought this long sword.

04:53.330 --> 04:55.370
It's impossible to maneuver.

05:04.840 --> 05:06.050
Hey.

05:06.130 --> 05:07.300
I'm okay.

05:07.390 --> 05:09.930
The blade hit the tree. It's just a cut.

05:13.230 --> 05:15.850
Why did you save me
when I was going to abandon you?

05:15.940 --> 05:17.730
You could have run away by yourself.

05:18.440 --> 05:20.230
I doubted you earlier.

05:20.820 --> 05:22.610
I can't apologize to you if you're dead.

05:23.530 --> 05:27.240
My mental fortitude is weak,

05:27.870 --> 05:30.200
and I don't have what it takes.

05:30.280 --> 05:31.950
In the future, I may doubt you again.

05:32.040 --> 05:33.620
But I promise,

05:33.700 --> 05:36.290
I will never betray you.

05:36.370 --> 05:37.210
What…

05:37.790 --> 05:40.290
I like escaping with you.

05:41.040 --> 05:42.590
With you and your tricks,

05:42.670 --> 05:46.930
I can escape from strong demons
I could never escape from on my own.

05:47.590 --> 05:51.100
Thinking about it that way,
I can't help but get excited.

05:51.970 --> 05:54.180
Even if you're ever cornered,

05:54.890 --> 05:56.520
or if you ever betray me,

05:57.770 --> 06:00.270
when we run away, we run together!

06:10.740 --> 06:14.700
<i>Tokiyuki has been betrayed</i>
<i>by countless people,</i>

06:15.870 --> 06:19.210
<i>but he has never betrayed anyone.</i>

06:20.920 --> 06:24.380
<i>At a time when betraying and deserting</i>
<i>one's allies was commonplace,</i>

06:24.880 --> 06:27.550
<i>Tokiyuki could be said to be</i>
<i>a devoted general.</i>

06:30.890 --> 06:33.850
Where are those thieves? Damn it.

06:33.930 --> 06:36.270
I can't see as well in the dark
at this age.

06:42.310 --> 06:43.320
Silly…

06:44.480 --> 06:45.900
I'm here for you.

06:48.360 --> 06:51.070
Oh, it's you, Ichikawa!

06:51.160 --> 06:52.530
<i>He's speaking to me casually?</i>

06:52.620 --> 06:54.080
With you by my side,

06:54.160 --> 06:57.080
we can kill all the thieves in the dark!

06:57.160 --> 06:59.670
<i>I'm older and of a higher rank than him.</i>

06:59.750 --> 07:02.040
<i>Why is he speaking to me so casually?</i>

07:05.420 --> 07:07.670
I've hidden some horses
at the end of these woods.

07:07.760 --> 07:08.760
We're almost there.

07:11.090 --> 07:12.180
Okay, let's go.

07:14.390 --> 07:18.100
<i>The bleeding isn't stopping.</i>
<i>He can't keep moving for much longer.</i>

07:27.650 --> 07:28.650
What?

07:28.740 --> 07:29.820
A thunderbolt?

07:30.570 --> 07:31.570
He's back.

07:32.610 --> 07:34.830
That's Sadamune's arrow.

07:35.530 --> 07:36.580
Don't be stupid.

07:36.660 --> 07:38.500
The sound of his horse
is about one meter away.

07:39.080 --> 07:41.750
In this pitch darkness,
he shouldn't be able to aim so accurately!

07:44.130 --> 07:46.500
<i>We still have some time</i>
<i>until we reach our horses.</i>

07:46.590 --> 07:49.340
<i>I can't outrun that arrow</i>
<i>with this kid with me.</i>

07:54.140 --> 07:55.220
<i>This damn brat.</i>

07:57.640 --> 08:00.640
Trust my ears and fire, Sadamune.

08:03.310 --> 08:07.190
I've entombed many in darkness
with these hands.

08:07.270 --> 08:09.280
Now, Sadamune.

08:09.360 --> 08:12.320
Shall we start off
by shooting down that wounded brat?

08:12.400 --> 08:13.860
Yes, Ichikawa.

08:13.950 --> 08:16.950
Show my arrow the way
with your perfect hearing.

08:17.620 --> 08:20.370
<i>If the obligation was invisible,</i>
<i>I could ignore it.</i>

08:20.450 --> 08:22.580
<i>But an obligation I can see?</i>

08:23.250 --> 08:25.080
<i>I have to repay it!</i>

08:28.090 --> 08:31.300
Are you two old geezers having fun?

08:32.300 --> 08:35.340
What a pain. But I'll take on both of you.

08:35.890 --> 08:37.680
Hmm? That fox mask.

08:37.760 --> 08:39.600
I've heard of it before.

08:39.680 --> 08:42.680
You're Genba Kazama, that thief's brat.

08:42.770 --> 08:43.770
Kazama?

08:43.850 --> 08:47.270
Yes. His father was disgraced
as a warrior for using unfair tactics,

08:47.360 --> 08:50.690
and so he was exiled from his clan.

08:50.780 --> 08:52.820
Then, he fell to thievery.

08:52.900 --> 08:56.320
Kazama is a branch
of the Suwa clan in Shinano…

08:57.070 --> 09:02.330
You've come under Yorishige's order
to steal the Imperial Command, huh?

09:02.410 --> 09:05.290
Imperial Command?
What are you talking about?

09:05.370 --> 09:10.090
I just thought
I'd make fun of you soldiers.

09:18.680 --> 09:21.350
Birds? I can't tell
where the sounds are coming from!

09:22.430 --> 09:25.140
I don't know about killing,
but morphing I know a thing or two about!

09:25.230 --> 09:28.770
And I won't stand losing
to you boring soldiers.

09:35.780 --> 09:37.280
No!

09:37.360 --> 09:38.700
Oh. Oh, no.

09:39.910 --> 09:42.740
You try to bewilder me
with your excessive movement!

09:44.160 --> 09:45.500
You underestimate me!

09:46.250 --> 09:48.130
You can't dodge me from this distance!

09:52.460 --> 09:53.630
Sadamune.

09:53.710 --> 09:54.630
-What?
-What?

09:55.590 --> 09:56.590
Take this!

09:59.010 --> 10:01.600
He cut my bowstring! That's unfair!

10:01.680 --> 10:03.060
Unfair?

10:07.690 --> 10:11.770
My accomplice loves these tricks.

10:11.860 --> 10:15.030
You can't appreciate them
because you're old,

10:15.110 --> 10:19.240
like the old and dusty documents
in that warehouse.

10:19.780 --> 10:22.870
So I told my accomplice, too…

10:24.750 --> 10:27.080
Paper isn't something to steal.

10:27.790 --> 10:29.790
It's more fun to burn.

10:39.720 --> 10:40.800
Oh?

10:50.400 --> 10:54.360
<i>The word "Shinobi" appears in one of</i>
<i>the oldest epics of Japan, the Taiheiki,</i>

10:54.440 --> 10:56.990
<i>which records the events of this time.</i>

10:58.150 --> 11:02.200
<i>"Bold and forthright" would begin to</i>
<i>disappear from the warrior's vocabulary.</i>

11:02.910 --> 11:08.250
<i>Those who can infiltrate like spies with</i>
<i>subversive tactics began to be prized.</i>

11:09.670 --> 11:11.210
<i>And thus, the ninja was born.</i>

11:15.920 --> 11:17.760
He disappeared?

11:18.470 --> 11:21.430
In the split second we were shocked
by the warehouse on fire!

11:21.930 --> 11:25.390
Sadamune. Could the Imperial Command
still be in there?

11:26.310 --> 11:29.350
We'll catch the wounded and make him
confess who the ringleader is!

11:29.430 --> 11:31.690
This sound of hooves.

11:32.190 --> 11:34.570
It's the two decoys running away!

11:41.990 --> 11:44.160
I can't catch up from this distance.

11:44.830 --> 11:50.750
That fox-masked brat tricked us all!

11:52.370 --> 11:54.250
I saw the signal to come,

11:54.330 --> 11:56.300
and look how our lord
is in such bad shape!

11:56.380 --> 12:00.470
Hey, Genba!
Be more careful with the Young Lord!

12:00.550 --> 12:01.930
Yeah, that's right!

12:02.010 --> 12:05.890
No, you guys. It's all thanks to Genba
we're able to outrun those two.

12:06.390 --> 12:07.680
It was fun.

12:08.350 --> 12:10.890
I hope we get to play hide-and-seek again.

12:12.810 --> 12:14.150
<i>My Genba.</i>

12:14.730 --> 12:19.110
<i>If you find a lord you'd like to serve</i>
<i>even without turning a profit,</i>

12:20.320 --> 12:21.860
<i>you should still take the money.</i>

12:22.360 --> 12:24.160
<i>Even if you plan on serving</i>
<i>till the next life,</i>

12:24.240 --> 12:25.530
<i>you should still take the money!</i>

12:32.540 --> 12:35.830
Fine. If I can have one province.

12:35.920 --> 12:38.750
I won't let you off the hook
if you don't pay.

12:38.840 --> 12:40.880
If you cannot pay,

12:40.960 --> 12:42.510
I'll track down your children,

12:42.590 --> 12:46.050
your grandchildren,
and all your relatives.

12:47.140 --> 12:52.560
That means you'll play tag
with my children too?

12:55.980 --> 12:57.360
That's not what I'm saying!

12:57.440 --> 13:00.360
I'm saying
you better take back the country!

13:00.440 --> 13:03.360
So you're saying you'll play with us
after we take back the country?

13:03.450 --> 13:05.610
Why are you like this?

13:05.700 --> 13:07.660
Come on, Genba. Stop moving!

13:07.740 --> 13:09.490
We're gonna collide!

13:13.500 --> 13:14.620
Go home!

13:14.710 --> 13:18.590
We won't clear out
if you don't have an Imperial Command.

13:18.670 --> 13:21.630
I bet you brutes are lying
about the Imperial Command

13:21.710 --> 13:23.800
so you can steal our land.

13:23.880 --> 13:26.970
That's right! I won't listen to someone
without an Imperial Command!

13:27.470 --> 13:29.970
If you're mad about it,
show me the Command!

13:34.770 --> 13:38.190
Damn those Suwa citizens.

13:39.020 --> 13:43.280
Fighting back uselessly. But I can get
another Imperial Command in a month!

13:43.360 --> 13:45.820
Your eviction notice is simply extended!

13:45.900 --> 13:47.280
There's bad news, my lord!

13:47.360 --> 13:50.280
We can't take the Suwa land anymore.

13:51.240 --> 13:55.040
What?

13:55.120 --> 13:58.670
KYOTO

13:58.750 --> 14:02.630
I took down the Kamakura shogunate.

14:02.710 --> 14:05.420
I took down about 1,000 important
retainers of the Kamakura shogunate.

14:07.510 --> 14:10.300
I commanded Takauji's rebellion.

14:10.390 --> 14:11.720
It was horrible.

14:11.810 --> 14:14.730
I had to fly back to the past with Buddha
and go on a journey.

14:15.310 --> 14:18.810
The majority are seeking reward, and
lying about their achievements to get it.

14:18.900 --> 14:22.440
It'll take years to determine
who's lying and who's telling the truth!

14:22.520 --> 14:25.440
We'll never get to discuss
our official duty.

14:29.780 --> 14:32.240
-What a pain!
-Sir!

14:32.330 --> 14:34.450
The Emperor said, "What a pain!"

14:34.950 --> 14:36.000
MAINTAIN STATUS QUO

14:36.080 --> 14:38.420
"Territories other than Hojo's
will remain as is.

14:39.080 --> 14:41.710
Suwa's will also remain undisputed."

14:44.090 --> 14:46.050
-This is infuriating!
-Let's be patient.

14:46.130 --> 14:47.800
Our chance will come, you know.

14:47.880 --> 14:50.800
You!

14:51.720 --> 14:52.890
<i>He is speaking to me casually?</i>

14:53.470 --> 14:56.060
Suwa!

14:57.850 --> 14:58.940
We did it!

14:59.020 --> 15:00.400
We're safe!

15:00.940 --> 15:03.400
Buying time really paid off.

15:03.480 --> 15:07.190
If we had simply handed our territory over
to Ogasawara,

15:07.860 --> 15:09.780
we'd never get it back.

15:10.490 --> 15:13.410
I must thank you for saving our land

15:13.490 --> 15:16.080
and also for securing a new,
dependable retainer.

15:18.000 --> 15:21.250
I feel better knowing Genba's
on our side now.

15:21.750 --> 15:25.210
-Though his personality is vulgar.
-Pour me more, pour me more!

15:28.130 --> 15:29.340
With his tricks,

15:29.420 --> 15:32.140
I could see him sneaking
into Takauji's sleeping quarters

15:32.220 --> 15:34.140
and slicing his head off just like that.

15:36.770 --> 15:41.100
That's impossible.
Takauji cannot be assassinated.

15:42.310 --> 15:44.440
Here is a good opportunity, Lord Tokiyuki.

15:44.520 --> 15:47.190
As I've said before,
you should know your enemy.

15:48.110 --> 15:50.030
Takauji Ashikaga is someone

15:50.740 --> 15:53.570
not even I can estimate.

16:07.710 --> 16:09.380
I see you've finally moved with a few men.

16:09.460 --> 16:10.720
EMPEROR GODAIGO'S SON
PRINCE MORIYOSHI

16:10.800 --> 16:12.510
But this shall be your grave.

16:12.590 --> 16:13.840
Your Highness,

16:14.340 --> 16:18.100
I reverently celebrate
your appointment as shogun.

16:19.020 --> 16:20.140
Your Highness,

16:20.230 --> 16:23.150
why do you have to keep coming
for my life?

16:24.480 --> 16:27.400
You are sure to betray
the Emperor one day.

16:27.480 --> 16:31.150
I will stain my hands
for the sake of my father!

16:33.200 --> 16:35.160
Protect the lord!

16:44.710 --> 16:46.840
The lower-ranked soldiers
don't stand a chance.

16:47.380 --> 16:51.220
Armed peasant thieves, monks,
and even rogue states.

16:51.880 --> 16:54.970
Those that follow him are indeed varied.
His charisma draws people in.

16:55.510 --> 16:57.350
Lord, allow me.

16:57.430 --> 16:59.680
No, the prince is after only me.

17:00.390 --> 17:03.600
If I speak to him one-on-one, I'm sure
we'll dissolve any misunderstandings.

17:04.900 --> 17:06.980
Is that okay, brother?

17:07.060 --> 17:08.320
It's no problem.

17:08.400 --> 17:11.030
It's merely the Imperial shogun
and rogues.

17:12.070 --> 17:13.070
Your Highness!

17:13.150 --> 17:15.280
-It's Takauji!
-Kill him!

17:26.460 --> 17:27.580
Please,

17:28.590 --> 17:29.630
settle down.

17:37.680 --> 17:39.260
Don't be intimidated! Go!

17:39.930 --> 17:41.270
Oops.

17:43.060 --> 17:44.600
There are many of you.

17:45.940 --> 17:47.600
<i>Takauji Ashikaga.</i>

17:48.650 --> 17:50.440
<i>My gut was right.</i>

17:51.360 --> 17:54.440
<i>You're a monster who shouldn't be</i>
<i>allowed to walk the planes of this life.</i>

17:55.860 --> 17:58.530
Oh, wait just a moment, Your Highness.

17:58.620 --> 18:01.240
We'll be alone soon enough.

18:18.180 --> 18:19.390
Right. That's done.

18:22.060 --> 18:24.930
Please trust me, Your Highness.

18:26.230 --> 18:29.020
I am loyal and devoted to the Emperor.

18:31.190 --> 18:33.190
<i>I couldn't win</i>
<i>if it were just me against him.</i>

18:33.940 --> 18:35.400
<i>But I'm not alone.</i>

18:36.030 --> 18:39.360
<i>If we combine everyone's efforts together,</i>
<i>then one day…</i>

18:39.450 --> 18:40.620
What's all this commotion?

18:41.990 --> 18:44.830
His Highness has unsheathed his sword.

18:47.750 --> 18:49.420
You guys. You came just in time.

18:50.000 --> 18:51.710
Hurry, we need reinforcements--

18:51.790 --> 18:52.920
It's Lord Takauji.

18:53.000 --> 18:54.210
It's Lord Takauji!

18:54.300 --> 18:56.380
It's Lord Takauji!

18:56.470 --> 18:58.260
It's actually Lord Takauji!

19:00.300 --> 19:02.140
Are you all right, my lord?

19:02.220 --> 19:03.760
Are you hurt?

19:03.850 --> 19:04.930
It's nothing too bad.

19:05.600 --> 19:06.810
Oh, I'm glad.

19:06.890 --> 19:08.060
Lord Takauji…

19:08.140 --> 19:10.730
I'm worried. Let's examine you
in the government office.

19:12.150 --> 19:15.530
My allies from yesterday…
Why are they over there?

19:19.780 --> 19:20.780
My Emperor.

19:20.860 --> 19:23.620
We cannot let that man in.

19:23.700 --> 19:26.620
Something not human writhes within him.

19:27.200 --> 19:28.330
Emperor!

19:29.960 --> 19:31.250
Emperor!

19:36.300 --> 19:39.300
Emperor!

19:40.630 --> 19:42.180
<i>Lord Takauji.</i>

19:43.760 --> 19:44.970
<i>Lord Takauji.</i>

19:45.470 --> 19:46.560
<i>Lord Takauji.</i>

19:46.640 --> 19:48.060
<i>Lord Takauji.</i>

19:49.100 --> 19:51.100
<i>Lord Takauji.</i>

19:51.190 --> 19:52.310
<i>Lord Takauji.</i>

19:54.060 --> 19:55.440
<i>Lord Takauji.</i>

19:56.110 --> 19:57.530
<i>Lord Takauji.</i>

19:57.610 --> 19:58.650
<i>Lord Takauji.</i>

19:59.240 --> 20:00.610
<i>Lord Takauji.</i>

20:00.700 --> 20:02.110
<i>Lord Takauji.</i>

20:03.490 --> 20:05.200
<i>Lord Takauji.</i>

20:07.700 --> 20:09.370
That happened in Kyo?

20:09.450 --> 20:12.080
He has military might,

20:12.170 --> 20:14.170
which makes it impossible
to assassinate him.

20:14.250 --> 20:16.630
He's also got an otherworldly charm.
That's Takauji Ashikaga.

20:17.250 --> 20:21.010
The person whose popularity
exceeds the Emperor's own son

20:21.800 --> 20:26.100
is a different beast
from the Takauji Ashikaga you know.

20:27.310 --> 20:28.890
Once again, Lord Tokiyuki,

20:29.890 --> 20:33.270
are you prepared to face an opponent
who stands at the top of this world?

20:39.230 --> 20:40.900
Young Lord!

20:44.620 --> 20:46.950
Help me with Genba!

20:48.490 --> 20:50.500
He's wasted
and touching shrine maidens' butts!

20:50.580 --> 20:52.750
And to top it off,
he's jumping around the room…

20:54.830 --> 20:57.170
-Swish, swish.
-People have drawn their swords

20:57.250 --> 21:01.130
because he's jumping around saying
he's gonna sprinkle pee everywhere!

21:01.220 --> 21:02.470
The story of the people at the top

21:02.550 --> 21:04.380
just turned into a story
about the people at the bottom.

21:04.470 --> 21:06.640
Shall we, my lord?

21:06.720 --> 21:09.720
We have to discipline this rude fox.

21:10.270 --> 21:11.270
Yes.

21:13.640 --> 21:15.020
Mr. Yorishige.

21:15.100 --> 21:16.690
You gave me allies.

21:16.770 --> 21:18.360
You gave me a way to fight.

21:18.440 --> 21:21.280
And you gave me self-confidence.

21:22.110 --> 21:24.910
They may still be small,
but they're all treasures you gave me

21:24.990 --> 21:28.120
that I'm proud of.

21:29.870 --> 21:33.080
No matter how much stronger Takauji is,
I won't give up.

21:33.160 --> 21:36.540
I'll collect more treasures
and try as many times as it takes!

21:39.250 --> 21:40.090
Hey, Genba!

21:40.170 --> 21:42.170
<i>Takauji and Tokiyuki.</i>

21:43.220 --> 21:46.640
<i>An invincible lion,</i>
<i>and a rabbit not even on his radar.</i>

21:46.720 --> 21:48.180
There! Get him!

21:48.680 --> 21:50.560
-Oh! Yeah, yeah, that's it!
-Over there!

21:53.930 --> 21:56.020
<i>The lion doesn't know yet</i>

21:57.100 --> 21:58.650
<i>that a day will come</i>

21:59.440 --> 22:01.480
<i>where he will fear the small rabbit.</i>

22:01.980 --> 22:04.950
Fluff fluff, fluff fluff, fluff fluff,
fluff fluff.

23:31.620 --> 23:33.620
Translated by Emily Walton

23:39.040 --> 23:39.870
EPISODE 7 (YEAR OF 1333)
CHILDREN IN WINTER

23:39.040 --> 23:39.870
Let's go!
